= Selection Protocol <sec:protocol>

Wave5 tested three interventions on the wave4 PP-TCN. Each was trained with the same recipe: an auxiliary *boundary* head (`boundary_tcn`), the short-spell loss (`short_tcn`), and heavier full-ball masking, 0.6 vs 0.3 (`masked_tcn`). These yield 12 probability families (each model alone, with the 25% GRU, ensembles and quality-weighted variants), which were crossed with 8 decoder variants for #sel.configurations configurations. Each configuration was evaluated on #sel.development_scenarios development scenarios from #sel.development_matches matches using #sel.short_tcn_grouped_folds grouped folds. All corruption rounds of a match leave the training set together, and normalisation and decoder statistics come from the training fold only. That is #sel.development_evaluations evaluations in total.

The objective is the *equal-provider mean spellF1*: conditions are averaged within each match first, then scores are averaged per provider. The adoption rule was written and hashed before fitting. A challenger replaces the wave4 control (`old_gru25/wave4`) only if it (a) gains at least #sel.minimum_gain, (b) wins at least #sel.minimum_winning_providers of 3 providers and (c) loses no more than #sel.maximum_provider_drop on any provider. The public GT was not read by the selection code. The external holdout and the public GT had both been seen in earlier campaigns, so this is adaptive research, not a fresh blind test.

= Results <sec:results>

== Development sweep

@fig:devgrid shows all 96 configurations. #N.dev_grid.n_eligible pass the adoption rule. The best, `short_gru25/dead45`, reaches #fx(N.dev_grid.best) against the control's #fx(N.dev_grid.control). With the decoder held fixed, the short-loss TCN beats the old PP-TCN (0.659 vs 0.650 with the wave4 decoder). The boundary head and the heavier masking do not beat the old PP-TCN. Removing the merge step (`no_merge`) is the single most damaging decoder change in every family, which confirms that sub-second flicker is the main failure mode under spellF1.

