== Per-provider and holdout behaviour

The development gain is uneven (@fig:prov, left). It is large on IDSSE (#sgn(N.provider.dev_sel.idsse - N.provider.dev_ctl.idsse)), moderate on Metrica (#sgn(N.provider.dev_sel.metrica - N.provider.dev_ctl.metrica)) and essentially zero on SkillCorner (#sgn(N.provider.dev_sel.skillcorner - N.provider.dev_ctl.skillcorner)). After the freeze, the holdout cohorts follow the same pattern (@fig:prov, right). IDSSE improves by #sgn(ho.at("IDSSE (2)").selected - ho.at("IDSSE (2)").previous_wave4) and Metrica Game 3 by #sgn(ho.at("Metrica G3 (2 cond.)").selected - ho.at("Metrica G3 (2 cond.)").previous_wave4), while clean SkillCorner is flat (#sgn(ho.at("SkillCorner (6) clean").selected - ho.at("SkillCorner (6) clean").previous_wave4)). Under the paired ball-drop stress the selected model is marginally *worse* (#sgn(ho.at("SkillCorner (6) stress").selected - ho.at("SkillCorner (6) stress").previous_wave4)) and wins only 2 of 6 matches.

== Where the gain comes from: possession length

@fig:recall breaks matched recall down by GT possession duration. Short-spell recall improves in every cohort. At IoU 0.75, for example, IDSSE rises from #(dr("IDSSE (2)", "previous_wave4", "lt_4s", "0.75").at(0))/#(dr("IDSSE (2)", "previous_wave4", "lt_4s", "0.75").at(1)) to #(dr("IDSSE (2)", "selected", "lt_4s", "0.75").at(0))/#(dr("IDSSE (2)", "selected", "lt_4s", "0.75").at(1)) and Metrica Game 3 from #(dr("Metrica G3 (2)", "previous_wave4", "lt_4s", "0.75").at(0)) to #(dr("Metrica G3 (2)", "selected", "lt_4s", "0.75").at(0)) of #(dr("Metrica G3 (2)", "selected", "lt_4s", "0.75").at(1)). Even so, short recall stays below 25% at that threshold. Under stress the gain is paid for elsewhere. Pooled precision at IoU 0.75 drops from 46.13% to 43.84% (1,613 → 1,713 predicted possessions, but only 744 → 751 matched), and recall of possessions lasting ≥ 15 s drops from 71.98% to 68.64%. Because the decoder changed together with the loss, this is a diagnosis of the whole pipeline, not an isolated effect of the loss weighting.

